# Build-context hygiene for the Docker build — same reasoning as
# api-gateway/.dockerignore (T014): without this, the local dev tree's own
# bin/obj output gets copied into the build context and can shadow/collide
# with what `dotnet publish` produces inside the container. Concretely: a
# Visual Studio restore on Windows bakes a Windows-only NuGet fallback path
# into obj/project.assets.json; COPY . . without this file would overwrite
# the container's own clean Linux restore with that stale, Windows-specific
# one, and `dotnet publish --no-restore` would fail trying to resolve it.
bin/
obj/
.vs/
